==Battleground==
*5 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*5 [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 33.33~50 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Heavenly Hippoe]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 53.33~80 seconds<sup>1,600f~2,400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Metal Hippoe]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 60~100 seconds<sup>1,800f~3,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Angelic Sleipnir]]s spawn after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>, delay 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Metal One Horn]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns.
**1 [[One Horn]] spawns.

==Strategy==
This stage looks extremely annoying on paper, but can easily be done using critical hitters such as [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]] or any other consistent critical hitter. You can bring meatshields such as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen/Artist Cat]] or Sumo Cat's true form, [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]], which is immune to knockback. You can also use other attackers along with your critical hitters to gradually deal damage to Angelic Sleipnir. For example, you can use a well-timed [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] if available, as well as other area attackers such as [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] or [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg/Paris Cat]] to deal with the Sleipnir over time. Collaboration units such as [[Felix the Cat Duke Cat (Special Cat)|Mercenary Leader Felix Cat]] can make this stage slightly easier, as his decent damage critical hits are able to one shot the Metal Hippoe and two shot the Metal One Horn.

